---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import { PORTAL } from '../data/site';
---

<Base
  title="Documentation"
  description="Where to find ServerPerch documentation: operator and user docs ship with the appliance; a versioned public docs site is planned."
>
  <section class="hero">
    <div class="container">
      <h1>Documentation</h1>
      <p class="lede">
        ServerPerch's operator and user documentation is maintained alongside the
        product and ships with the appliance itself.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <div class="container prose">
      <h2>Today</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>
          <strong>In the product:</strong> the appliance ships its operator and user
          guides — install, licensing, updates and policies, monitoring, PKI and
          enrolment, security, backup/restore and troubleshooting — so the docs always
          match the version you are running, including on air-gapped networks.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>In the portal:</strong> your
          <a href={PORTAL.root}>customer portal</a> account gives you licence keys,
          activation management and appliance downloads (OVA, VHDX, qcow2) with
          checksums and signatures.
        </li>
        <li>
          <strong>Evaluating?</strong> The <a href="/features">features</a> and
          <a href="/security">security</a> pages cover the platform's shape; a
          <a href={PORTAL.signup}>trial account</a> is the fastest way to read the
          real docs — they ship inside the trial appliance.
        </li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Coming</h2>
      <p>
        A public, versioned documentation site (<code>docs.serverperch.com</code>) is
        on the release roadmap. Until it is published this page is the canonical
        pointer — if you need a specific document before then,
        <a href="/contact">contact us</a> and we'll send it.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Base>
